What this port changed
----------------------

The port keeps the original's task, reward, observations, graph network,
TD3 update, hindsight relabelling, replay rules and evaluation metrics, and
rewrites them for PyTorch and mjlab. It changes the following.
docs/DESIGN.md, sections 12 to 17, and docs/evidence/differences.verified.md
give each change with its reason and its measured effect.

- Simulator. C MuJoCo stepped by 64 asynchronous CPU actors, with a Reverb
  replay, became mjlab and MuJoCo Warp on a GPU, running kinematics and
  collision only. All worlds step in lockstep and the replay stays on the GPU.
- Framework. JAX and Flax became PyTorch. The rounding of the original's
  bf16 learner is re-created. Repeated target and obstacle embeddings are
  computed once.
- Robot model. The default arm is the Panda represented by 36 collision
  spheres, with a straight stick in place of the gripper and tool, TCP at
  0.160 m. The original's mesh arm and tool remain as the `mesh_tool` option.
- Scenes. Start states are regenerated by the port's own sampler and inverse
  kinematics, as `.pt` pools. The original's `.pb` start states and the
  paper's tasksets can still be read.
- Evaluation. The stored rotation of the static obstacle boxes, inverted in
  the original, is corrected. Evaluation runs inside the training process,
  with more episodes per evaluation.
- Agents. FastTD3, the main agent, SAC and PPO were added beside the
  reproduced TD3 agent.


Modified files
--------------

As Apache 2.0 section 4(b) asks, these parts of the package are modified
versions of the original, changed as described above. Paths are relative to
src/roboballet_mjlab/. The code cites the original's file and line where
behaviour is surprising.

  env/                 environments/planning_env.py, base_env.py, target.py
  scenes/              environments/planning_env.py, geometry.py, target.py,
                       mujoco_simulator.py
  agent/               agents/compute_features.py, agents/networks.py,
                       train/train.py
  replay/              agents/actor.py, train/stats.py, launch/launch.py
  train/               agents/actor.py, agents/evaluator.py, train/train.py,
                       launch/launch.py
  config.py            launch/hparams.py, environments/base_env.py,
                       agents/actor.py
  structs.py           environments/planning_env.py
  data/static_boxes/, data/scenes/*_static*.pt
                       The archive's static evaluation world: the obstacle
                       boxes of its decomposition, frozen. The pools built
                       from them correct the boxes' rotation. The
                       *_static_paper pools also hold the archive's paper
                       tasksets.
  assets/panda_spheres_stick.xml
                       The archive's
                       data/mujoco_world/assets/franka_emika_panda/panda_nohand.xml,
                       itself a modified copy of MuJoCo Menagerie's
                       franka_emika_panda model. Collision spheres and a
                       stick were added. The meshes it references are
                       Menagerie's.


